request: Make the output easier to read.

governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" could mean many different changes, and I can't turn it into a testable contract without more detail. Changing the output will probably also change behaviour that the existing format tests check, so I need to know exactly what you want.)
governor asks: What should the new output look like? Could you show an example line or two? Some options:
(1) Status markers: use checkboxes like "[ ]" / "[x]" for open and done todos.
(2) Alignment: pad the IDs so the titles line up in a column, e.g. "  3. [ ] Buy milk".
(3) Due dates: show them in a set place, e.g. "(due 2024-05-01)" at the end of the line.
(4) Empty list: show a message like "No todos." when there's nothing to list.
(5) Summary: add a footer like "2 open, 1 done".
(6) Colour: highlight done or overdue items with ANSI colours.
Which of these do you want? Or what else? Should the output of the add and complete commands change too, or only list?

